{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571647064,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MDk4MTUxMjg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3820","origin":"github"},"title":"`git status` broken in submodule with adjusted branch (on crippled FS)","message":"I was trying to figure out, how we could properly save the state of a modified subdataset in a parent repository when both are using adjusted branches. However, I stumbled upon behavior that seems like a more fundamental bug. Here is a demo:\n\nPrepare a repo with a submodule\n\n```\n/tmp % datalad create repo\n/tmp % datalad create -d repo repo/sub\n/tmp % echo 123 \u003e repo/sub/file\n/tmp % echo 234 \u003e repo/file\n/tmp % datalad save -d repo -r\n\n# clean state\n/tmp % git -C repo submodule\n fdb2afee57643a978494530b136a8ced7f6d5f34 sub (heads/master)\n\n/tmp % git -C repo/sub log -n1 |cat\ncommit fdb2afee57643a978494530b136a8ced7f6d5f34\nAuthor: Michael Hanke \u003cmichael.hanke@gmail.com\u003e\nDate:   Mon Oct 21 09:37:04 2019 +0200\n\n    [DATALAD] Recorded changes\n/tmp % git -C repo status\nOn branch master\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\n```\n\nClone onto a crippled FS and initial both repos\n\n```\n/tmp/crippled % git clone /tmp/repo\nCloning into 'repo'...\ndone.\n/tmp/crippled % cd repo\n/tmp/crippled/repo (git)-[master] % git annex init\ninit  \n  Detected a filesystem without fifo support.\n\n  Disabling ssh connection caching.\n\n  Detected a crippled filesystem.\n(merging origin/git-annex into git-annex...)\n(recording state in git...)\n(scanning for unlocked files...)\n\n  Entering an adjusted branch where files are unlocked as this filesystem does not support locked files.\n\nSwitched to branch 'adjusted/master(unlocked)'\nok\n(recording state in git...)\n\n/tmp/crippled/repo (git)-[adjusted/master(unlocked)] % git submodule init\nSubmodule 'sub' (/tmp/repo/sub) registered for path 'sub'\n\n/tmp/crippled/repo (git)-[adjusted/master(unlocked)] % git status\nOn branch adjusted/master(unlocked)\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\n\n/tmp/crippled/repo (git)-[adjusted/master(unlocked)] % git -C sub annex init\ninit  \n  Detected a filesystem without fifo support.\n\n  Disabling ssh connection caching.\n\n  Detected a crippled filesystem.\n(scanning for unlocked files...)\nok\n```\n\nThe repo is reported clean, despite the submodule checkout not being identical with the recorded commit:\n\n```\n/tmp/crippled/repo (git)-[adjusted/master(unlocked)] % git status\nOn branch adjusted/master(unlocked)\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\n\n/tmp/crippled/repo (git)-[adjusted/master(unlocked)] % git submodule\n fdb2afee57643a978494530b136a8ced7f6d5f34 sub\n/tmp/crippled/repo (git)-[adjusted/master(unlocked)] % git -C sub log -n1 |cat\ncommit 3aac9c0887b2eb6e47f0da33e07656a70c32434e\nAuthor: Michael Hanke \u003cmichael.hanke@gmail.com\u003e\nDate:   Mon Oct 21 09:37:04 2019 +0200\n\n    git-annex adjusted branch\n```\n\nInitially I thought this is a nice feature, and it detects that there is nothing different other than the adjustment. However, no modifications to the submodule are being detected:\n\n```\n/tmp/crippled/repo (git)-[adjusted/master(unlocked)] % touch sub/this\n/tmp/crippled/repo (git)-[adjusted/master(unlocked)] % git status\nOn branch adjusted/master(unlocked)\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\n```\n\nBut modifications to the parent are being detected:\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/crippled/repo (git)-[adjusted/master(unlocked)] % touch up\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/crippled/repo (git)-[adjusted/master(unlocked)] % git status\nOn branch adjusted/master(unlocked)\nUntracked files:\n  (use \"git add \u003cfile\u003e...\" to include in what will be committed)\n\n        up\n\nnothing added to commit but untracked files present (use \"git add\" to track)\n```\n\nIt seems as if Git doesn't realize that it is in a submodule, as it reports the parent change from inside the submodule, but still not the original modification\n\n```\n/tmp/crippled/repo (git)-[adjusted/master(unlocked)] % git -C sub status\nOn branch adjusted/master(unlocked)\nUntracked files:\n  (use \"git add \u003cfile\u003e...\" to include in what will be committed)\n\n        ../up\n\nnothing added to commit but untracked files present (use \"git add\" to track)\n```\n\nWhen I apply the same modifications to the original repositories on the normal FS, everything behaves as expected:\n\n```\n/tmp/repo (git)-[master] % touch sub/this\n/tmp/repo (git)-[master] % touch up\n/tmp/repo (git)-[master] % git status\nOn branch master\nChanges not staged for commit:\n  (use \"git add \u003cfile\u003e...\" to update what will be committed)\n  (use \"git checkout -- \u003cfile\u003e...\" to discard changes in working directory)\n  (commit or discard the untracked or modified content in submodules)\n\n        modified:   sub (untracked content)\n\nUntracked files:\n  (use \"git add \u003cfile\u003e...\" to include in what will be committed)\n\n        up\n\nno changes added to commit (use \"git add\" and/or \"git commit -a\")\n/tmp/repo (git)-[master] % git -C sub status\nOn branch master\nUntracked files:\n  (use \"git add \u003cfile\u003e...\" to include in what will be committed)\n\n        this\n\nnothing added to commit but untracked files present (use \"git add\" to track)\n```\n\n@joeyh Could you please have a look and share your thoughts on what is happening here?","files":null}]}